AI-ASSISTED AUTHORSHIP. The chapters in this book were drafted by
Claude, an artificial intelligence language model produced by
Anthropic, PBC, working against an indexed corpus under detailed
instructions from the author. The author selected the sources,
designed the chapter structure, set the editorial framing, and made
all decisions about what to include and exclude. The AI performed the
drafting, cross-referencing, and quotation against the corpus. No
fact-checking outside the corpus was performed. Verifiability is
bounded by the corpus. Readers who object to AI-assisted writing on
principle are advised that this work is unsuitable for them.

